/**
 * Wrangler config for the AEC Integrations web app (SSR Worker).
 *
 * SSR Worker scaffolded in AECI-21. Hono handles `/api/*`; everything else
 * falls through to Angular SSR (`@angular/ssr`). `nodejs_compat` is required
 * for the SSR runtime (Node polyfills used by `@angular/ssr`); see
 * `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/CICD_PLAN.md` §4.1.
 *
 * Tiers (promotion order): preview → staging → demo → production.
 *   - Web production serves the apex `aecintegrations.com` + `www.` (the public
 *     home) AND `prod.aecintegrations.com` (the Access-gated internal host). The
 *     apex cutover (AECI-247/277) moved apex + www off the retired landing Worker
 *     onto this Worker; the bare apex 301s to `www.` in the SSR Worker (`www.` is
 *     the canonical served host — ADR 0011 amendment 2026-07-05).
 *   - Web demo serves `demo.aecintegrations.com` (the public showcase tier).
 *   - Preview deploys use `workers_dev` URLs per PR; staging is
 *     `staging.aecintegrations.com`.
 * All tiers share ONE Supabase auth project (ADR 0017); per-environment
 * isolation is via Cloudflare Access, not project separation.
 *
 * The `services` bindings (`API`) call the private API Worker (`apps/api/`)
 * over Cloudflare's internal RPC fabric — the API has no public ingress.
 * See docs/STAGE_1_SPEC.md §6.2, §15.2 and docs/CICD_PLAN.md §4.2.
 *
 * Edge cache, KV, and cookie-stripping middleware land in subsequent
 * Phase 1 issues.
 *
 * Datadog (AECI-31) — secrets, NOT vars, so values stay out of git. Push per
 * env with `wrangler secret put <KEY> --env <preview|production>`:
 *   DD_APPLICATION_ID   client-exposed RUM application id (rendered into HTML)
 *   DD_CLIENT_TOKEN     client-exposed RUM client token   (rendered into HTML)
 *   DD_API_KEY          server-only; Datadog Logs HTTP intake
 *   DD_SITE             public; defaults to datadoghq.com when unset
 *
 * Cache purge (AECI-56 / Phase 2.10; native Workers Cache since WC-6 / AECI-320):
 *   ADMIN_PURGE_TOKEN   secret; bearer the caller of POST /admin/purge presents
 *   CF_PURGE_API_TOKEN  secret; legacy CF API token (Zone.Cache Purge on
 *                       aecintegrations.com ONLY). No longer read by /admin/purge
 *                       after WC-6; pruned in WC-10 (AECI-324)
 *   CF_ZONE_ID          public var; formerly the purge target zone. Unused on
 *                       this Worker after WC-6; pruned in WC-10 (AECI-324)
 *
 * Algolia search (AECI-134) — secrets, NOT vars (values stay out of git). Both
 * are client-exposed (rendered into HTML by injectAlgoliaBootstrap), but the
 * SEARCH key is query-only + index-scoped. The admin/management key is NEVER
 * set on this Worker (it would reach the browser):
 *   ALGOLIA_APP_ID      shared app id (rendered into HTML)
 *   ALGOLIA_SEARCH_KEY  per-env query-only search key (rendered into HTML)
 * Provision per env with `node scripts/algolia/provision.mjs`; see
 * docs/CICD_PLAN.md §7.5 and docs/environments.md §6/§8.
 *
 * Supabase auth (AECI-193 / Phase 5.2):
 *   SUPABASE_URL        public var — the SINGLE shared auth project across all
 *                       environments (ADR 0017); same value in every `vars` below
 *   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   publishable/anon key for that single shared project.
 *                       Secret (NOT a var) only to keep values out of git —
 *                       same convention as ALGOLIA_SEARCH_KEY. CI pushes the
 *                       single un-suffixed `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` GH secret after
 *                       deploy (same value for every env — ADR 0017; warn-and-skip
 *                       when absent this phase; flips to REQUIRED in 5.5). It must
 *                       match SUPABASE_URL's project or the browser sign-in fails
 *                       with `Invalid API key`. The service-role key is NEVER set
 *                       on any Worker (AUTH_AND_RLS.md §3).
 *
 * Push secrets per env (`wrangler secret put`). (`CF_ZONE_ID` / `CF_PURGE_API_TOKEN`
 * are unused on this Worker after WC-6 and are pruned in WC-10 (AECI-324).)
 */
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "aeci-web",
  "account_id": "e62ec9d8012c3e0c225f8e4dbab76b79",
  "main": "./dist/server/server.mjs",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-10",
  // `nodejs_compat` — @angular/ssr Node polyfills (see the header note).
  // `ctx.exports` is default-on for this compatibility date. Do not add the retired
  // `enable_ctx_exports` flag: current workerd rejects that redundant opt-in at startup.
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true,
  },
  "dev": {
    "port": 8788,
  },
  "assets": {
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "directory": "./dist/browser",
  },
  "env": {
    "preview": {
      "name": "aeci-web",
      "workers_dev": true,
      "observability": { "enabled": true },
      // WC-3 (AECI-317) + WC-4 (AECI-318) — native Cloudflare Workers Cache via
      // the two-entrypoint gateway pattern (ADR 0020 §2). The `default` export is
      // a cache-key-normalizing gateway with its OWN cache DISABLED (so it runs on
      // every request: strips utm_*/non-allowlisted params, canonicalizes order,
      // then forwards a normalized `cf.cacheKey` to `Renderer`); `Renderer` is the
      // cached SSR entrypoint — the platform stores its response from
      // `Cache-Control` and serves future HITs without running the render. Set
      // per-env, NEVER at top level (so a bare `wrangler dev` stays uncached).
      // Caching is live on preview + staging only; `demo`/`production` ship the
      // same two-entrypoint code but stay UNCACHED (no `cache`/`exports` block)
      // until WC-8 (noindex-on-HIT) lands (ADR 0020 §1). WC-5 (queue purge, AECI-319)
      // + WC-6 (native /admin/purge, AECI-320) are DONE: the cross-Worker purge queue
      // consumer is wired per-env on staging/demo/production below (`queues.consumers`;
      // none on preview) and, because the cache lives on `Renderer`, delegates the
      // `ctx.cache.purge()` into that entrypoint via the `ctx.exports` loopback
      // (ADR 0020 §2/§3). `cross_version_cache` left at the
      // default (per-version isolation ⇒ each deploy cold-starts the cache, so a
      // template change is live on the first post-deploy request — ADR 0020 §5).
      "exports": {
        "default": { "type": "worker", "cache": { "enabled": false } },
        "Renderer": { "type": "worker", "cache": { "enabled": true } },
      },
      // COMMIT_SHA / DEPLOYED_AT are sentinels overridden by `wrangler deploy
      // --var` in CI (AECI-92 /_version, AECI-74 parity with apps/api).
      "vars": {
        "ENV": "preview",
        // Crawler-indexing gate (apps/web/src/server/robots-policy.ts).
        // FAIL-CLOSED — anything but "true" blocks indexing via the
        // X-Robots-Tag: noindex header (plus a sitemap-less robots.txt that
        // still allows crawling, so the noindex is actually seen and honored).
        // Pre-launch this stays "false" on EVERY env, including production —
        // demo.aecintegrations.com is gated by Cloudflare Access until launch
        // (ADR 0017) and must not be indexed yet either way. At public launch,
        // set the indexable env's value to "true". Do NOT key off ENV:
        // production is the pre-launch demo.
        "ALLOW_INDEXING": "false",
        "DD_SITE": "us5.datadoghq.com",
        "COMMIT_SHA": "unknown",
        "DEPLOYED_AT": "1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        // AECI-193 / ADR 0017: Supabase base URL (public). The SINGLE shared
        // auth project — identical across preview/staging/production. Pairs with
        // the CI-pushed SUPABASE_ANON_KEY secret — see the header comment.
        "SUPABASE_URL": "https://ktuhnlypztujpsseujzx.supabase.co",
        // AECI-239: PostHog ingestion host (public; US Cloud). The CSP
        // connect-src is pinned to the US hosts. The POSTHOG_KEY is a CI-pushed
        // secret (absent → analytics no-ops, fail-open).
        "POSTHOG_HOST": "https://us.i.posthog.com",
      },
      "services": [{ "binding": "API", "service": "aeci-api-preview" }],
    },
    "staging": {
      "name": "aeci-web-staging",
      "vars": {
        "ENV": "staging",
        // See the preview env's note. Staging is behind Access AND non-indexable.
        "ALLOW_INDEXING": "false",
        "DD_SITE": "us5.datadoghq.com",
        "COMMIT_SHA": "unknown",
        "DEPLOYED_AT": "1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "SUPABASE_URL": "https://ktuhnlypztujpsseujzx.supabase.co",
        "POSTHOG_HOST": "https://us.i.posthog.com",
      },
      "observability": { "enabled": true },
      // WC-3 (AECI-317) + WC-4 (AECI-318) — native Workers Cache via the gateway
      // (`default`, cache off) + cached `Renderer` entrypoint pair. See the preview
      // env note above; staging is the pre-prod validation tier for the "preview →
      // staging first" rollout (ADR 0020 §1). demo/production remain uncached until
      // WC-8. The WC-5 purge queue consumer is wired just below (`queues.consumers`).
      "exports": {
        "default": { "type": "worker", "cache": { "enabled": false } },
        "Renderer": { "type": "worker", "cache": { "enabled": true } },
      },
      "routes": [
        {
          "pattern": "staging.aecintegrations.com",
          "custom_domain": true,
        },
      ],
      "services": [{ "binding": "API", "service": "aeci-api-staging" }],
      // WC-5 (AECI-319): consume the cross-Worker cache-purge queue. The API Worker
      // (producer) enqueues on promote/moderation; this Worker issues `ctx.cache.purge()`
      // (ADR 0020 §3). Consumer only — no producer here. The queue is provisioned before
      // this deploy by the idempotent `create_queue` step in deploy.yml.
      "queues": {
        "consumers": [
          {
            "queue": "aeci-cache-purge-staging",
            "max_batch_size": 1,
            "max_retries": 3,
            "max_concurrency": 1,
          },
        ],
      },
    },
    "demo": {
      "name": "aeci-web-demo",
      "vars": {
        "ENV": "demo",
        // Public (NOT behind Access), pre-launch — no-index. Keep "false". See
        // the preview env's note; `indexingAllowed` keys off this, not `ENV`.
        "ALLOW_INDEXING": "false",
        "DD_SITE": "us5.datadoghq.com",
        "COMMIT_SHA": "unknown",
        "DEPLOYED_AT": "1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        // ADR 0017: the single shared auth project (same value in every env).
        "SUPABASE_URL": "https://ktuhnlypztujpsseujzx.supabase.co",
        "POSTHOG_HOST": "https://us.i.posthog.com",
      },
      "observability": { "enabled": true },
      // WC-4 (AECI-318): ships the gateway + `Renderer` two-entrypoint code like
      // every env, but caching stays OFF here (no `cache`/`exports` block) — the
      // gateway still forwards to `Renderer`, just uncached. WC-4/5/6 are in; enable
      // (add the preview-style `exports` block) only once WC-8 (noindex-on-HIT) lands
      // (ADR 0020 §1).
      // The public showcase tier. `custom_domain: true` makes wrangler reconcile
      // the demo.aecintegrations.com DNS record + cert on deploy — on the first
      // demo deploy it REASSIGNS that hostname off the old production Worker, so
      // deploy demo BEFORE re-deploying production onto prod.aecintegrations.com.
      "routes": [
        {
          "pattern": "demo.aecintegrations.com",
          "custom_domain": true,
        },
      ],
      "services": [{ "binding": "API", "service": "aeci-api-demo" }],
      // WC-5 (AECI-319): consume the cross-Worker cache-purge queue (see the staging
      // note). Registered here ahead of `cache.enabled` (still gated on WC-8): with
      // no cache yet, the `Renderer.purgeCache()` delegate returns null so the consumer
      // no-ops each message (`outcome:no_cache`) and acks — fully wired for when WC-8
      // flips the cache on. Provisioned by promote-to-demo.yml.
      "queues": {
        "consumers": [
          {
            "queue": "aeci-cache-purge-demo",
            "max_batch_size": 1,
            "max_retries": 3,
            "max_concurrency": 1,
          },
        ],
      },
    },
    "production": {
      "name": "aeci-web-production",
      "vars": {
        "ENV": "production",
        // AECI-247/277 apex cutover: the app is the public home, so indexing is
        // ON. Removes `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` + makes robots.txt/sitemap.xml
        // crawlable (server-runtime.ts). The Access-gated `prod.` internal host
        // stays crawler-free via Cloudflare Access (docs/access.md), so a single
        // ALLOW_INDEXING="true" doesn't leak a duplicate index. Provision the
        // launch-only SEO secrets (INDEXNOW_KEY, GOOGLE_INDEXING_SA_*) at the same
        // time — pinging for a noindex site is a bug (docs/launch-cutover-runbook.md).
        "ALLOW_INDEXING": "true",
        "DD_SITE": "us5.datadoghq.com",
        "COMMIT_SHA": "unknown",
        "DEPLOYED_AT": "1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "SUPABASE_URL": "https://ktuhnlypztujpsseujzx.supabase.co",
        "POSTHOG_HOST": "https://us.i.posthog.com",
      },
      "observability": { "enabled": true },
      // WC-4 (AECI-318): ships the gateway + `Renderer` two-entrypoint code, but
      // caching stays OFF here (no `cache`/`exports` block) until WC-8 lands (WC-4/5/6
      // are in) (ADR 0020 §1) — see the preview env note.
      // AECI-247/277 apex cutover. Web prod now serves the public apex
      // `aecintegrations.com` + `www.` AND the Access-gated internal
      // `prod.aecintegrations.com`. `custom_domain: true` makes wrangler reconcile
      // the DNS record + cert on the aecintegrations.com zone on deploy — for the
      // apex + www it REASSIGNS the hostnames off the (retired) landing Worker onto
      // this one (same mechanism environments.md relies on for demo.). THIS IS THE
      // DNS FLIP: the next promote-to-prod deploy after this merges makes the app
      // the live apex. The bare apex 301s to `www.` inside the SSR Worker (`www.` is
      // the canonical served host — ADR 0011 amendment 2026-07-05).
      "routes": [
        {
          "pattern": "aecintegrations.com",
          "custom_domain": true,
        },
        {
          "pattern": "www.aecintegrations.com",
          "custom_domain": true,
        },
        {
          "pattern": "prod.aecintegrations.com",
          "custom_domain": true,
        },
      ],
      "services": [{ "binding": "API", "service": "aeci-api-production" }],
      // WC-5 (AECI-319): consume the cross-Worker cache-purge queue (see the staging
      // note). Registered ahead of `cache.enabled` (still gated on WC-8): with no
      // cache yet, the `Renderer.purgeCache()` delegate returns null so the consumer
      // no-ops each message (`outcome:no_cache`) and acks. Provisioned by promote-to-prod.yml.
      "queues": {
        "consumers": [
          {
            "queue": "aeci-cache-purge-production",
            "max_batch_size": 1,
            "max_retries": 3,
            "max_concurrency": 1,
          },
        ],
      },
    },
  },
}
